    <hr class="section-divider">

    <h2>3.2 Existing System Data Flow (DFD Overview)</h2>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li><strong>1. Initiate Transaction:</strong> User submits request via USSD (*247#) or Mobile App[cite: 1].</li>
      <li><strong>2. Verify PIN / OTP:</strong> Security authentication verifies identity against Customer Info datastores[cite: 1].</li>
      <li><strong>3. Process Transaction:</strong> Balance adjustments are applied across the Balance/Ledger DB[cite: 1].</li>
      <li><strong>4. Update Ledger:</strong> Status logs are written to the centralized Transaction Log file[cite: 1].</li>
      <li><strong>5. Send Confirmation:</strong> SMS and push confirmations are routed to both customer and merchant terminals[cite: 1].</li>
    </ul>

    <hr class="section-divider">

